# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
# Checkpoints of a Python simulation (D223) on the CPU in
# mixed precision, scenario cli-to-python of Inputs/python_checkpoints.py.
# `mdir run` stops at step 10 and a Python simulation continues its
# checkpoint to step 20: the state, the energy file, and the trajectory
# equal those of the run that did not stop, to the bit (NVE, NVT, and NPT
# with PME and constraints). The NVT run gives `neighbor_capacity` to both
# front ends, an entry of both fingerprints (D227):
# no warning, and one when the Python model leaves it out.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_checkpoints.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Mixed mdir %t cli-to-python | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: mdir run -> Python NVE CPU Mixed
# CHECK: neighbor_capacity = 480 in both: no warning; in one: a warning
# CHECK: mdir run -> Python NVT CPU Mixed
# CHECK: mdir run -> Python NPT CPU Mixed
# CHECK: checkpoints cli-to-python CPU Mixed passed
